# Line endings are decided HERE, not by each contributor's git config.
#
# `.editorconfig` already asks EDITORS for LF; this asks GIT for it, which is the half
# that was missing. A clone with `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default, and easy to
# end up with anywhere — rewrites LF to CRLF on every checkout, so a file keeps coming
# back with endings nobody chose: `prettier --check` then reports the whole file as
# unformatted, and a `git stash` round-trip is enough to undo a `prettier --write`.
# README.md had drifted that way and was the only CRLF file in the repo.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content for itself, so `*` is safe as a blanket rule.
* text=auto eol=lf
